From: Oever Gonzalez <software@notengobattery.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7996: add an NPU offload restart knob

When the NPU's handoff queue to the wireless side wedges, every packet
it dequeues is rejected with HOSTADPT_API_Q_FULL and TO_HOSTAPD_COUNT
stops advancing, while the driver looks idle and the tx token pool sits
nearly empty. Reloading the module clears it, which narrows the corrupt
state to what the offload handshake re-establishes -- but a reload costs
the radios, renumbers the wiphy and orphans a page pool, so it is a poor
instrument for deciding which half is at fault.

The L1 SER path already stops and re-initialises exactly that handshake
without touching the wireless chip. Expose the same pair, so a wedge can
be answered in place: if re-running it unblocks the queue, the fault is
in the offload binding rather than in NPU firmware state, and the fix
belongs there.

Write-only, and it reports both step results, so a stop that times out
against an unresponsive NPU is distinguishable from a clean restart.

--- a/mt7996/debugfs.c
+++ b/mt7996/debugfs.c
@@ -46,6 +46,31 @@ static int
 DEFINE_DEBUGFS_ATTRIBUTE(fops_implicit_txbf, mt7996_implicit_txbf_get,
 			 mt7996_implicit_txbf_set, "%lld\n");
 
+static int
+mt7996_npu_restart_set(void *data, u64 val)
+{
+	struct mt7996_dev *dev = data;
+	int stop_err, init_err;
+
+	if (!mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76))
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	/* the L1 SER path's pair, without the chip reset around it */
+	stop_err = mt7996_npu_hw_stop(dev);
+
+	mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+	init_err = __mt7996_npu_hw_init(dev);
+	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+
+	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev, "npu offload restart: stop=%d init=%d\n",
+		 stop_err, init_err);
+
+	return init_err;
+}
+
+DEFINE_DEBUGFS_ATTRIBUTE(fops_npu_restart, NULL, mt7996_npu_restart_set,
+			 "%lld\n");
+
 /* test knob of system error recovery */
 static ssize_t
 mt7996_sys_recovery_set(struct file *file, const char __user *user_buf,
@@ -927,4 +952,6 @@ int mt7996_init_debugfs(struct mt7996_de
 	debugfs_create_file("implicit_txbf", 0600, dir, dev,
 			    &fops_implicit_txbf);
+	debugfs_create_file("npu_restart", 0200, dir, dev,
+			    &fops_npu_restart);
 	debugfs_create_devm_seqfile(dev->mt76.dev, "twt_stats", dir,
 				    mt7996_twt_stats);
